```console
$ redkiln answer --help
Answer an open human gate, by the option its question declared

Usage: redkiln answer [OPTIONS] --explain-sufficed <yes|no> --toml-opened <yes|no> <ITEM> <OPTION>

Arguments:
  <ITEM>    The item whose gate is open
  <OPTION>  The option id, as the gate's question declared it

Options:
      --attach <KIND=PATH>         An artifact the chosen option admits, as KIND=PATH; repeatable
  -C <PATH>                        Act on the repository at this path instead of the working directory
      --explain-sufficed <yes|no>  Did reading the explanation suffice to decide? [possible values: yes, no]
      --toml-opened <yes|no>       Was the item's own file opened before deciding? [possible values: yes, no]
  -h, --help                       Print help

```
